    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full suite is green with `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the disposable-domain blocklist rejection in the email validation path.\n\n**Change** \u2014 `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/validation/EmailNormalizer.java`:\n- Added a `DISPOSABLE_DOMAINS` set containing `mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, and `guerrillamail.com`.\n- After the existing syntax check, `normalize` now extracts the domain (from the lower-cased address) and throws `InvalidEmailException` if it's on the blocklist.\n\n**Why this location:** `EmailNormalizer.normalize` is the single choke point used by both the add and update owner flows (`OwnerRestControllerV1`), and `InvalidEmailException` is already mapped to `400 Bad Request` by `ExceptionControllerAdvice`. So the rejection applies consistently to create and update with no new wiring needed. The `null` case (email is optional) is preserved untouched.\n\nThe new `errorRejectsDisposableDomain` acceptance test passes, and the full suite builds green.",
