    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change fits the existing unit naturally. `EmailNormalizer` was already a validation-and-normalization utility that raises `InvalidEmailException` (mapped to 400) for a supplied-but-invalid address, so adding the disposable-domain rejection here is additive and coherent rather than introducing a new concern in the wrong place. The blocklist is a private `static final Set.of(...)` constant sitting right next to the existing `EMAIL_PATTERN` constant, matching the established idiom, and it carries a Javadoc consistent with its neighbor. The check is correctly ordered after syntactic validation and after lower-casing, so the domain comparison against the lower-cased constants is sound, and the class/method Javadoc were both updated to reflect the new behavior. Nothing is duplicated and the method has not become a catch-all.",
